# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CATENA / VAIDYAM — environment for Next.js (Vercel free tier) +
#                     PostgreSQL (Supabase free tier)
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# In Vercel, add the same keys under Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables. Only DATABASE_URL is required — every other key is optional and
# the API degrades gracefully (with a clearly labelled fallback in the
# dashboard's provenance strip) when it is absent. Nothing ever throws.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — PostgreSQL connection (local Postgres or Supabase)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev default (matches the bundled docker/local Postgres):
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/app_db
#
# Supabase (free tier) — Project → Settings → Database → Connection string
# (use the "Session pooler" / URI form, port 5432 or 6543):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:<password>@<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — Supabase REST (only needed if you also want the JS/REST client
# used by src/lib/vaidyam/supabase.ts; the app works fully on DATABASE_URL
# alone via Drizzle). Get these from Supabase → Settings → API.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — Nutrition panel (USDA FoodData Central)
# Affects: /api/nutrition (dashboard → Nutrition view)
# Get it (free, instant, no card): https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup
# Without it: a deterministic per-food estimator is used and labelled
# non-live in the provenance strip. Do NOT use the literal "DEMO_KEY" — it is
# globally rate-limited (HTTP 429) so it is treated the same as "no key".
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# USDA_API_KEY=

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — LLM providers for the Agent Swarm + Draft/Verify Cascade
# Affects: /api/swarm, /api/cascade, /api/health, /api/saas
# Without any of these, the swarm runs a deterministic graph reasoner over
# the personal causal graph — every panel still renders real numbers.
# Any ONE of the four below is enough. Resolution order (src/lib/vaidyam/
# inference.ts → providers()): groq → nim → openrouter → proxy.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GroqCloud LPU — drafts (fastest; generous free tier): https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# NVIDIA NIM — verifier for divergent spans: https://build.nvidia.com/
# NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter — Agent-Forest voting pool (has :free models): https://openrouter.ai/keys
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Generic OpenAI-compatible proxy (any OpenAI-shaped endpoint). Set BOTH.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What is LIVE without any key at all (no signup, CORS-open, free):
#   Open-Meteo weather ........... api.open-meteo.com
#   Open-Meteo air quality ....... air-quality-api.open-meteo.com
#   openFDA adverse events ....... api.fda.gov
#   Europe PMC literature ........ www.ebi.ac.uk (PubMed mirror)
#   Population health ............ disease.sh
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
